  "name": null,
  "problem": "A certain company produces $2$ types of flour, flour $A$ and flour $B.$ The following table describes how the number of consumers changes between both types of flour each month:\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"10\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td colspan=\"2\" align=\"center\">From:</td> \n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td width=\"80\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\"><b>Flour $A$</b></td>\n<td width=\"80\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\"><b>Flour $B$</b></td> \n</tr>\n<tr> \n<td rowspan=\"2\" align=\"center\">To:</td>\n<td width=\"80\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\"><b>Flour $A$</b></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.3$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.6$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr> \n<td width=\"80\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\"><b>Flour $B$</b></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.7$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.4$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n\nThat is, $70%$ of flour $A$ customers switch to flour $B$ each month, and $60%$ of flour $B$ customers change to flour $A.$\n\nCurrently, $6\\,000$ customers use flour $A,$ while $4\\,000$ customers use flour $B.$ How many customers will use flour $A$ in one month? You may assume that the total number of customers doesn't change.",
  "worked_solution": "",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
